WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.213 --> 00:00:03.213
(slow techno music)

00:00:04.848 --> 00:00:08.176
- A lot of the work is quite repetitive.

00:00:08.176 --> 00:00:11.873
The pleats took about two months to do.

00:00:11.873 --> 00:00:15.264
Probably did those eyes 10 times.

00:00:15.264 --> 00:00:18.480
Even the texture of the skin.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.647
They're graceful, dancing,
which I wanted to portray.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:25.680
That's the whole goal,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.847
is to make them feel like
they're gonna swim away.

00:00:35.115 --> 00:00:38.619
I'm Stephen Kesler, also known as Tusk.

00:00:38.619 --> 00:00:41.702
I'm a large scale wildlife sculptor.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.288
I found sculpture a little later in life.

00:00:46.288 --> 00:00:47.936
In my late 30s.

00:00:47.936 --> 00:00:49.744
Moving from one career to the other,

00:00:49.744 --> 00:00:51.096
especially into the art world,

00:00:51.096 --> 00:00:54.161
that's totally scary
and foolish thing to do.

00:00:54.161 --> 00:00:56.744
I don't think I had an option
after I started sculpting.

00:00:56.744 --> 00:01:00.911
I think my life was going to
be it, no matter what I did.

00:01:04.136 --> 00:01:07.219
Sculpture as a whole has inspired me.

00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:10.821
I mean it's a 24 hour thing for me.

00:01:10.821 --> 00:01:13.738
Sleep just gets in the way, almost.

00:01:15.965 --> 00:01:16.902
When I'm out,

00:01:16.902 --> 00:01:19.941
doing day-to-day things not being here,

00:01:19.941 --> 00:01:23.119
it's always running through my head.

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:25.486
I don't know if I'd personally
call myself a daydreamer,

00:01:25.486 --> 00:01:28.486
but I could probably be labeled one.

00:01:34.287 --> 00:01:37.620
There is definitely a calming with clay.

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:41.189
I usually work 12 hours,

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:43.189
for three days straight.

00:01:44.045 --> 00:01:45.805
Being able to realize

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.805
what I want in it, quickly,

00:01:48.805 --> 00:01:53.405
it just seems like it works
together with how I process.

00:01:53.405 --> 00:01:57.773
I've been involved with making
three life size giraffes,

00:01:57.773 --> 00:02:00.221
40 foot whale shark,

00:02:00.221 --> 00:02:02.041
four Manta rays,

00:02:02.041 --> 00:02:05.041
and we're working on this 30 foot iguana

00:02:05.041 --> 00:02:05.874
behind me.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:10.250
(fast pulsing music)

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:14.218
The humpback whales took
roughly nine months.

00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:17.002
The inspiration to do these
pieces for the aquarium

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:20.085
was because Utah is a landlocked state.

00:02:21.994 --> 00:02:23.346
There's a limited number of people

00:02:23.346 --> 00:02:26.281
who see these in real life anyways.

00:02:26.281 --> 00:02:28.547
To be able to be in the same room,

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.369
feel the size of it.

00:02:30.369 --> 00:02:32.041
Hopefully there's an energy to it.

00:02:32.041 --> 00:02:34.689
And hopefully inspire conservation acts,

00:02:34.689 --> 00:02:36.417
because of it.

00:02:36.417 --> 00:02:37.793
If someone says, "Oh, I can't sculpt."

00:02:37.793 --> 00:02:38.737
I said, "Have you tried?

00:02:38.737 --> 00:02:39.570
"Buy it."

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:40.977
You never know what's gonna happen.

00:02:40.977 --> 00:02:42.289
Open the box of clay.

00:02:42.289 --> 00:02:43.570
See what's in it, you know?

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:47.403
There might be a humpback
whale in the future.

